{"catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","hits":[{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#phr","id":"shared.glossary.phr","summary":"The application a patient uses to see consent requests and to approve, deny or revoke them.","title":"PHR, personal health record application","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/p3/endpoints/p3-subscription-hiu/06-p3-post-subscription-requests-v3-hiu-care-context-on-notify#p3-subscription-hiu-on-notify","id":"hiecm.endpoint.p3-subscription-hiu-on-notify","summary":"Tell ABDM you received a new record notification under a subscription.","title":"Acknowledge a new record notification","type":"endpoint"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#gateway","id":"shared.glossary.gateway","summary":"The component that routes calls between participants so they never call each other directly. It is not the consent manager, and no health record passes throu...","title":"Gateway, the routing layer between participants","type":"glossary"},{"doc_url":"/docs/uhi/v1/getting-started/going-live#2-record-a-demo-and-request-sign-off","id":"uhi.sandbox.demo-sign-off","summary":"Record your app running the service's flow and send it to your NHA point of contact. Sign-off arrives in writing.","title":"Record a demo and request UHI sign-off","type":"sandbox"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/milestones/p3#phr-subscriptions","id":"hiecm.concept.phr-subscriptions","summary":"A subscription tells a personal health record app when a record is linked to a person's address, and the person must agree to it first.","title":"Subscriptions, and why a personal health record application needs one","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"","id":"shared.fhir.document-bundles","summary":"Every ABDM health record travels as one FHIR document Bundle: a Composition first, eight possible NRCES profiles, and a two tier validation story. This atom ...","title":"FHIR document bundles, the eight ABDM record types","type":"fhir"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/how-it-fits#roles","id":"hiecm.concept.roles","summary":"Your role, IMS or PHR, is fixed by the entity your software acts for, while HIP and HIU change with the direction each record moves.","title":"Roles, which entity your software acts for and which way the record moves","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-callbacks/08-m2-post-v3-consent-request-hip-notify#m3-on-consent-request-notify-hip","id":"hiecm.callback.m3-on-consent-request-notify-hip","summary":"ABDM tells the HIP that a consent covering its records was granted, revoked or expired.","title":"The patient's decision, sent to the record holder","type":"callback"},{"doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/concepts/consent#consent-in-a-phr-app","id":"hiecm.concept.consent-in-a-phr-app","summary":"A personal health record app must let a person see a consent request, change it, allow or refuse it, see what is allowed, and take it back.","title":"The five things a personal health record application must let a person do with consent","type":"concept"},{"doc_url":"/docs/nhcx/v1/reference/error-codes#payr","id":"nhcx.error.payr-1059","summary":"The payer rejected your preauthorisation or claim because an attached clinical record or observation points at the wrong kind of record for its visit.","title":"PAYR-1059, a clinical record points at something other than an encounter","type":"error"}]}
